WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.702
This debate today.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:06.606
It's about who gets to be an American.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.909
What opinions do we get to have

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.212
Do we have to have to be counted

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.747
as Americans?

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.915
This is what this debate is about.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.550
Madam Speaker,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.053
there is this idea that you are a suspect

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.155
if you are an immigrant

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.391
or if you are from certain parts

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:24.991
of the world

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:28.028
or a certain skin tone or a Muslim.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.563
It is no accident

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.398
that members

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.966
of the Republican Party

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:36.002
accused the first black president,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.838
Barack Obama, of being a secret Muslim.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.275
It is no accident that former

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.977
President Donald Trump

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.212
let a birther movement

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.549
that falsely claimed he was born in Kenya

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.386
because to them, falsely labeling

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.187
the first

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.522
and only

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.190
president of the United

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.391
States of America,

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.960
a Muslim, an African immigrant,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.763
somehow made him less American.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.131
Well,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.101
I am Muslim.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.469
I am an immigrant.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.805
And interestingly from Africa,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.311
Is anyone surprised

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.647
that I am being targeted?

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:23.650
Is anyone surprised that I am somehow

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.151
deemed unworthy

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.620
to speak about American foreign policy

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.457
or that they see me

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.991
as a powerful voice

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.327
that needs to be silenced

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.663
Frankly, it is expected

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.465
because when you push power,

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.967
power pushes back,

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.403
representation matters

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.739
continuing to expand our ideas of

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.741
who is American

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.143
and who can partake

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.278
in the American experience

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.314
experiment is a good thing.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:58.618
I am an American, an American

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.820
who was sent here

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.791
an American who was sent here

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.993
by her constituents

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.529
to represent them in Congress.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:10.797
A refugee

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.566
who survived the horrors of a civil war.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.402
Someone who spent her childhood

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.171
in a refugee camp.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.906
Someone who knows what it means

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.940
to have a shot

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.142
at a better life

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.043
here in the United States.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.545
And someone who believes

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.046
in the American dream

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.815
and the American possibility

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:32.318
and the promise and the ability

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.988
to participate in the democratic process.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.224
That is what this debate is about.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.361
There is an idea out there that I am not

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.263
that I do not have

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.332
objective decision making because of who

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.767
I am, where I come from,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.502
and my perspective.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.138
But I reject that We say

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.340
there is nothing objective

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.109
about policymaking.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.711
We all inject our perspective,

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.046
our point of views,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.981
our lived experi alliances

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.050
and the voices of our constituents.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.986
That's what democracy is about.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.055
So what is the work

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.890
of the Foreign Affairs Committee?

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.927
It is not to cosign the stated foreign

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:16.229
policy of whatever administration

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.430
is in power.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.265
It's about oversight.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.466
It's the critique

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.534
And to advocate

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.403
for a better path forward.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.804
But most importantly,

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.506
it is to make the myth

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.740
that American foreign

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.477
policy is intrinsically moral a reality.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:34.080
So I will continue to speak up

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:37.350
because representation matters.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.485
I will continue to speak up

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.020
for little kids

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.022
who wonder who is speaking up for them.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.858
I will continue to speak up for families

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.927
around the world who are seeking justice,

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:49.262
whether they are

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.631
displaced in refugee camps

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.601
or they are hiding under their beds

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:56.402
somewhere.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.136
Like I

00:03:57.136 --> 00:04:00.073
was waiting for the bullets to stop

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.810
because this child

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.680
survivor of war would have wanted that.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.883
The nine year old me

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.886
would be disappointed

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.555
if I didn't talk

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.790
about the victims of conflict.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.559
Those that are experiencing

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.761
unjust wars, atrocities,

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.862
ethnic cleansing,

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.832
occupation or displacement like I did.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.434
They are looking

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.536
to the international community

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.806
and the United States asking for help.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.241
They look to us

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.143
because the international community

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:40.246
and the United States profess the values

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.015
of protecting human rights

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.484
and upholding international law.

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:46.819
So we owe it to them not to make this

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:50.123
a myth, but a reality.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:53.226
I didn't come to Congress to be silent.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.495
I came to Congress to be their voice,

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.330
and my leadership and voice

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.532
will not be diminished.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.768
If I am not on this committee

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.436
for one term.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:06.572
My voice will get louder and stronger

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:07.940
and my leadership

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.876
will be celebrated around

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.511
the world as it has been.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.415
So take your vote or not.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.318
I am here to stay

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:22.322
and I am here to be a voice against harms

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.057
around the world and advocate

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:25.391
for a better world.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.292
I yield back.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.060
Ilhan Omar

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.194
speaking a fiery

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.462
address, a defiant speech

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:29.896
on the floor

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:30.963
of the House of Representatives.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.166
The Republican led House is about to vote

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.334
to kick her off the House

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.201
Foreign Affairs Committee.

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.769
She says it is retribution.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.937
She says it is unfair

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.605
she says it is un-American,

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.607
but she says it is no surprise to her.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:42.675
Tracing Donald Trump's

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.143
support of the birther movement.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:45.812
The Republicans who said Barack

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:48.247
Obama as president was secretly a Muslim.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.115
Let's get to our chief

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.917
congressional correspondent, Manu Raju.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:51.851
Mano this vote.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:52.885
You just heard the defiance

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:53.853
from Congressman Omar.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.220
The vote

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.688
that will take place in moments

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.423
is a key test of the new speaker

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.291
Kevin McCarthy.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.226
He has a very narrow majority

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.694
and many of his members are

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:02.929
a little squishy about this

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:05.898
Yeah, no question about it.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.967
He can only lose four Republican votes

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.535
in order to allow this

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.037
this to succeed,

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:12.438
to kick her off of the House

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.473
Foreign Affairs Committee.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.374
And he has been moving

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.241
behind the scenes

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.142
over the last several days

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:16.876
to shore up

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.412
concerns, concerns about this tit for tat

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.180
that has occurred after Democrats moved

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.415
to Republicans off

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.483
of their committee assignments

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:24.584
last Congress.

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:27.286
McCarthy vowing some retribution of sorts

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.221
for Ilhan Omar.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.722
Ever since that happened here

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:30.790
and a lot of Republicans

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.391
agreeing with them,

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:32.925
but some concern about it.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:33.860
But behind the scenes,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.828
McCarthy has locked up the votes.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.562
He has indicated that

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:37.463
he has made sure

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:38.965
that his members are in line.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:39.932
Just moments ago,

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.267
Congresswoman Nancy Mace,

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.201
who is one who has said

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:42.735
that she would

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:43.703
oppose this

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:44.904
because of her concern

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:45.872
about the precedent

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.140
this would set by setting

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:47.607
King off

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.841
another member of the committee,

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.176
expanding a precedent

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.210
from the last Congress.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.044
She said she's actually

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:52.979
going to vote for this

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:54.414
because she got an agreement

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.081
from the speaker

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.183
to figure out a new process going forward

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.218
to allow members to appeal any effort

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.953
to try to kick them off of the committee.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.288
There's going to be some language

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:03.689
change to the resolution here.

